<title>JAPAN: Japan Sept crude imports down 4.4 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</title>
<headline>Japan Sept crude imports down 4.4 pct yr/yr -- MITI.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of International</p>
<p>Trade and Industry (MITI) on Friday issued the following data</p>
<p>on crude oil imports during September 1996:</p>
<p> CRUDE OIL   (1,000 kl) (1,000 bbl) mth/mth% yr/yr%</p>
<p> Iran	   2,559	 16,096    +19.5    +99.7</p>
<p> Saudi Arabia 3,366	 21,172    -33.2    -13.3</p>
<p> Kuwait	   905	  5,692    -28.3    -37.7</p>
<p> Neutral Zone 1,287	  8,095    +23.7    - 7.0</p>
<p> Qatar	  1,365	  8,586    -22.9    -10.9</p>
<p> Oman	     965	  6,070    -41.3    -33.6</p>
<p> UAE	    5,177	 32,563    -21.2    - 7.6</p>
<p> Yemen	    354	  2,227    +156.9   +106.6</p>
<p> U.S.A.	   127	    799    - 38.4    ---</p>
<p> China	  1,455	  9,152    + 15.7   + 19.4</p>
<p> Malaysia	 270	  1,698    - 56.6   - 47.1</p>
<p> Brunei	   253	  1,591    + 15.4   +  9.4</p>
<p> Indonesia    1,248	  7,850    - 30.7   - 12.8</p>
<p> Vietnam	  340	  2,139    - 41.5   - 16.7</p>
<p> Mexico	   291	  1,830    - 48.7   - 48.3</p>
<p> Africa	   238	  1,497    + 43.2    ----</p>
<p> Australia	 74	    465    - 43.2   - 22.5</p>
<p> TOTAL	 20,274	127,523    - 19.4   -  4.4</p>
</text>
